      "projects": [
        {
          "title": "Unmask",
          "subtitle": "Sep 2020 - Present",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Unmask is an educational web application that brings light to the tragedies and injustices happening around the world through unlawful activities. Whether it be the illegal gold mining happening in Peru to the trafficking of illegal substances and weapons in most of Asia and South America, these activities often get overlooked at the expense of the lives of innocent victims that were caught up in the middle of this at no fault of their own.\n\nWhile there is estimated to be 44 trillion gigabytes worth of data circulating throughout the internet, highly important information as such often either gets buried by search engine algorithms or is displayed through an old user interface that more than often loses the interests of the user. To mitigate this, we have effectively combined tools that not only provide accurate information all in one place but also enhance the user experience such that it promotes a higher retention rate."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Microsoft HoloLens Mixed Reality Chess",
          "subtitle": "Aug 2019 - Nov 2019",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Project Grandmaster came to be as a demonstrative and research purposes to create a design that incorporates limit-free mechanism in a virtual environment that is interacted within the real world, using Microsoft’s Mixed Reality Toolkit (MRTK) and HoloLens 2, allowing the users to experience the best of two worlds.\n\nProject Grandmaster focuses on the advanced hand tracking of the HL2 device, utilising this capability to provide a chess experience as close to a real chess game as possible. Allowing the user to manipulate the pieces with their hands as though they were real pieces placed directly in front.\n\nThe game also takes advantage of it being in a digital environment with features that provide visual assistance such as displaying possible moves and other useful visual tips. Project Grandmaster aims to integrate the best qualities from both real chess and digital chess into one experience."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
